# D-105 slice 1 (the author's Q39, 2026-09-27; steps/d105-index-table.md §5), under --walk-methods:
# `Other` writes Model's two size_t fields in the other order.  The walked root passes its field
# `o: Other` to `rd (Model: m)` and `wr (Model: m; size_t: v)`: admitted by NAME -- the correspondence
# table goes with the value into the arena's `implements` table (lmx_walk_admit_as), and `m\a` is read
# and written at Other's slot for `a`.  `mm: Model` goes to the same formal as Model's own
# (admitted with no table).  Without the table `m\a` read Model's slot 0 -- Other's `b`, 20 (D-105).
# Success is 7.
Model:
    size_t: a 1U
    size_t: b 2U
end: Model
Other:
    size_t: b 20U
    size_t: a 10U
end: Other
fn: rd (Model: m) size_t
return: m\a
fn: wr (Model: m; size_t: v) size_t
    m\a: v
    return: m\b
o: merge: Other
mm: merge: Model
size_t: got 0U
int: ok 7
got: rd(o)
if: got != 10U
    ok: 1
got: rd(mm)
if: got != 1U
    ok: 2
got: wr(o 11U)
if: got != 20U
    ok: 3
if: o\a != 11U
    ok: 4
if: o\b != 20U
    ok: 5
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
